






The dimdi or Dumid is a traditional percussion instrument, a hand-framed drum popular in South Asian folk and devotional music, closely resembling the Kanjira or Dumki.

Whereas Gudum is a traditional percussion instrument, which is an iron-framed drum covered in animal skin, performed primarily by communities like Gond, Baiga in Chhattisgarh.

Another instrument, Kinnari or Kinnari Veena, is a stringed instrument which is like a tube or a stick string instrument with gourd resonators.


